WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.460
Speaker 1: We have new polling and it is it
is remarkable.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:09.330
It has been 15 years since Americans were
as optimistic about the future of the country

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.070
as they are today.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:15.610
To new polls again confirm some things that
we already knew.

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:21.600
Americans largely approve of Joe Biden's performance
as president so far, but the polls were also

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.530
asking about American optimism more generally.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:30.590
And an ABC Ipsos poll finds that almost two
thirds of Americans are optimistic about the

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.340
next year.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:37.899
Americans have not been this optimistic about
the year to come since two thousand six per

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:40.219
the same ABC poll.

00:00:40.219 --> 00:00:42.630
A second poll released by Yahoo!

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:48.430
News and YouGov finds that 57 percent of the
country approves of Joe Biden's handling of

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.720
the pandemic.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:55.250
When asked if Biden's performance was better,
worse or the same than expected, the plurality

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.079
39 percent, said Biden is doing even better
than expected.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:00.470
Twenty eight percent said worse.

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.840
Twenty four percent said about what we expected.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.979
And overall, Joe Biden has a fifty four percent
approval rating.

00:01:05.979 --> 00:01:08.880
Now, you and I might see that in, say, fifty
four.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.539
That's not that's not so good.

00:01:10.539 --> 00:01:12.350
That's not a very high number.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:19.039
Remember that Donald Trump never hit 50 percent,
even on a single day of his presidency and

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:25.280
was plagued by approval in the 30s for the
most part, and even twenty nine percent when

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.280
he left office.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.610
So this this is a change for sure.

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:35.960
Now, in terms of the country being divided,
this is this is interesting and not great

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.579
numbers for Joe Biden.

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:43.499
Twenty eight percent of Americans believe
that the country is more divided since Joe

00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:44.499
Biden took office.

00:01:44.499 --> 00:01:46.899
Twenty three percent believe it is.

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:47.899
I'm sorry.

00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:49.630
Twenty three percent say more divided.

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:53.530
Twenty eight percent say less divided.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.389
That is interesting because everybody's blaming
Biden.

00:01:57.389 --> 00:01:59.299
The people that think the country is more
united.

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:01.630
I think it's more united because of Joe Biden.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.049
The people that think the country is more
divided also think it's more divided because

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:06.479
of Joe Biden.

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:11.709
But what's clear is that overall politics
has become a lot more boring and people seem

00:02:11.709 --> 00:02:13.489
to be OK with that.

00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:18.920
Now, fascinatingly, there was the assumption
that because things would be boring under

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.150
Joe Biden, shows like The David Pakman Show
wouldn't do well.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.360
In fact, there were gleeful.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.920
Trump is saying, David, when Trump is gone,
your show will be circling the drain, which

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.480
is a phrase we've been hearing for 15 years
that we keep growing.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.190
But put that aside for a second.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:36.110
I assumed we would we would see a decline
in viewership.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:39.409
Corporate media has seen a big decline in
viewership since Trump has left.

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:43.579
But then something I really don't understand
happened because I was prepared for like a

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:49.450
full year of really things being pretty slow
in late March, then early April, mid-April,

00:02:49.450 --> 00:02:51.439
April just finished.

00:02:51.439 --> 00:02:54.099
The numbers came that back very strong.

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:58.150
There were no Biden scandals, nothing in the
Biden administration even coming close to

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:02.569
the insanity of the Trump White House, and
yet that dip we saw that we see after every

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.989
election in January and February and early
March, it's almost completely recovered.

00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:13.430
We were back up to 30 million views in April,
12 million views on Facebook.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:15.560
These are like 20, 20 numbers once again.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.519
So I'm curious what you think is going on,
because things are kind of boring in a sort

00:03:20.519 --> 00:03:25.420
of salacious from a salacious evaluation type
standpoint.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.519
TV networks are reporting significantly lower
ratings.

00:03:28.519 --> 00:03:30.670
Trump, no doubt, was good for ratings.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:31.670
And yet.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:35.980
We're almost back to where we were in December,
which was a record month, not all the way,

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.860
maybe eighty five percent of the way there,
if you look at what did best in April.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:44.640
There's some Trump stuff in there that's left
over that he's still doing things, but it's

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.799
a lot of other things.

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:49.180
Clip's about right wingers who just call into
the show to talk to him.

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:50.180
He did really well.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.349
The Matt Gate scandal got a lot of attention.

00:03:52.349 --> 00:03:57.900
Critiques of right wing media framing did
well reporting on some of these corporate

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:02.769
scams, Foxconn and others, coverage of the
Derik Shervin trial, stories about vaccine

00:04:02.769 --> 00:04:04.500
conspiracies and other things.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.530
At this point, there's like seven or eight
different general areas of content that are

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:10.739
doing very well.

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:12.120
So something is going on.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:17.340
It's not only that people are more optimistic
than they've been for 15 years, they're optimistic,

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.530
but they're also not tuning out.

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.639
If it bleeds, it leads.

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:22.910
You know, we know about that.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:28.050
If people are satisfied and complacent rather
than panicked, they tend to watch a lot less

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.050
news.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:32.370
But yet people are watching almost as much
of the show as they were in December.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.310
The most optimistic interpretation I have
is people recognize that things are going

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:42.440
in the right direction, but realize that if
we tune out now and not pay attention to what's

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.600
going on, maybe we get Trump or something
like him back in twenty twenty for the real

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:47.600
explanation.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.169
Could be anything I'd be curious to hear from,
from you.

00:04:50.169 --> 00:04:54.590
Why is most of that election peak audience
already back?

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:55.590
Let me know your thoughts.

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.910
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:58.570
Very interested in hearing from.

